WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:06.600
The 30th movie in the Marvel Cinematic Universe is&nbsp;
a moving, fond farewell to a hero – but it's also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:11.460
the start of something new. Warning: spoilers&nbsp;
ahead for "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever."&nbsp;

00:00:11.517 --> 00:00:13.261
"You can come and find out."

00:00:13.261 --> 00:00:14.940
"Black Panther: Wakanda Forever" 

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.320
deals heavily with the fallout around the&nbsp;
untimely death of the nation's King T'Challa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:24.660
a development which mirrors the tragic, real-life&nbsp;
passing of actor Chadwick Boseman. In that way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:28.860
the film very much continues the tradition&nbsp;
of Marvel Phase 4 films dealing to some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:34.020
extent with the themes of grief and loss.
However, while no one will forget T'Challa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.580
or Boseman any time soon, the "Black Panther"&nbsp;
sequel also makes it clear there are other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:43.860
heroes out there who can serve to usher in&nbsp;
the future of the MCU. Nowhere is this more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:48.720
evident than in the introduction of new&nbsp;
character Riri Williams, aka Ironheart.&nbsp;

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:54.000
In "Wakanda Forever," Riri is a dedicated&nbsp;
and driven college student at MIT with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.140
penchant for creating ingenious high-tech&nbsp;
devices that get co-opted by the government,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:02.040
like a vibranium detection device that&nbsp;
proves crucial to the movie's plot.&nbsp;

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:07.200
Fortunately, the authorities haven't yet gotten&nbsp;
their hands on her pièce de résistance — the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.375
Ironheart armor.

00:01:08.609 --> 00:01:12.281
"I am warning&nbsp;you, do not take another step toward me."

00:01:12.608 --> 00:01:14.788
"See how they teach the children to treat their guests."

00:01:14.788 --> 00:01:15.502
After making a 

00:01:15.502 --> 00:01:19.680
big impression on the big screen, Riri&nbsp;
will return for her own Disney+ series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:24.480
appropriately titled "Ironheart." While there's&nbsp;
still much we don't know about the show, we can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.620
glean a few things about where it's probably&nbsp;
going from the ending of "Wakanda Forever."&nbsp;

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:33.000
When we're first introduced to Riri Williams,&nbsp;
she's a 19-year-old college student, trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.620
juggle a normal life with very abnormal interests.&nbsp;
It's safe to say the show will likely take place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:42.360
in large part on this college campus, seeing&nbsp;
Riri juggle the task of building her Ironheart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:47.220
armor with her attempts to be a regular student.&nbsp;
We also get a bit of her backstory in the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:51.000
as she reveals that her relationship with her&nbsp;
father fostered her interest in engineering.&nbsp;

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.680
Outside of Riri's story, Marvel has already&nbsp;
confirmed that a villain named The Hood will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:00.660
function as an antagonist in the "Ironheart"&nbsp;
series. However, Riri will also likely go up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:05.460
against another barrier along her solo journey.&nbsp;
In a key piece of dialogue featured in "Wakanda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:10.740
Forever," Riri bemoans the fact that as a young&nbsp;
Black girl, she's rarely taken as seriously as she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:15.960
should be, despite her remarkable intelligence.&nbsp;
It'd be a safe bet Riri will face similar problems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:20.460
in "Ironheart," and have to overcome them as&nbsp;
a part of her growth as a person and a hero.&nbsp;

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:24.840
One thing that will have to happen in the&nbsp;
"Ironheart" series is this new heroine will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:29.580
have to get herself a new suit of armor. There&nbsp;
are two Ironheart suits Riri Williams wears in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:33.900
"Black Panther: Wakanda Forever." The first&nbsp;
is a rough prototype Riri's forced to deploy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:38.100
when government officials close in on her&nbsp;
garage. However, for the film's final battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:43.320
Riri gets one heck of an upgrade with an Ironheart&nbsp;
suit she makes courtesy of Wakandan technology.&nbsp;

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:48.180
While it's a pretty slick suit, it turns out&nbsp;
that Riri can't keep it. At the end of the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:52.740
Shuri tells Riri that while she's free to&nbsp;
return to MIT, the new Ironheart suit has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:57.420
to remain in Wakanda. It makes sense; Wakanda&nbsp;
isn't exactly in a safe position on the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:02.040
stage by the movie's conclusion, so the Wakandans&nbsp;
probably don't want their revolutionary technology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:06.660
to be seen on such a wide scale just yet.
As a result, one of the first things that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:11.160
probably going to take place in the "Ironheart"&nbsp;
show is Riri designing a new set of armor for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:16.140
her to wear. The Hood is a formidable opponent&nbsp;
who uses magic, so Riri's going to need to use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:20.460
all of her wits to come up with something that&nbsp;
can match him in combat. While all these details&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:24.360
paint a rough picture of what to expect with&nbsp;
"Ironheart," there's still plenty left that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:28.080
will be a big surprise. We'll just have to&nbsp;
wait and see what the series has in store.

